# The adversarial corpus fixtures are byte-exact by design: the homoglyphs,
# zero-width characters, bidi controls and encodings in them ARE the test.
# -text disables every form of line-ending normalisation and working-tree
# conversion, so what is committed is what the scanner sees on every
# platform. Marking them diff=nodiff would hide the content in review, so
# they stay diffable -- only the conversion is switched off.
testdata/adversarial-corpus/malicious/** -text
testdata/adversarial-corpus/benign/** -text
